<HubLayout
  title="Food & Water"
  seoTitle="Emergency food supply and water storage: how much to keep"
  description="How much food and water to store for an emergency, how to keep it fresh and how to make doubtful water safer. Free calculators and UK-focused guides."
  intro="Start with 3 days of food and water for everyone at home, pets included."
  tone="water"
  art="water-storage"
  guideCategories={['water', 'food']}
  toolSlugs={['water-storage-calculator', 'food-storage-calculator', 'food-rotation-tracker', 'emergency-cooking-calculator', 'long-term-food-planner', 'rainwater-collection-calculator']}
>
  <Fragment slot="why">
    <p>Water and food are the foundations of any emergency plan. Mains water and supermarkets are very reliable, but a burst main, a flood or heavy snow can interrupt them for a few days, and shops can sell out quickly.</p>
    <p>Once you have 3 days of each, build up from there at your own pace.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <p slot="after" class="mt-2 measure">Choosing a filter? Read our <a href="/gear/how-to-choose-a-water-filter/">guide to emergency water filters</a>.</p>
</HubLayout>
